      "reason": "The task mixes native-grid global means with regridded map comparisons, so this fragment applies because native grids should be used for integrals/means over each model’s own domain and regridding only for maps and pattern comparisons.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute the first requested global means on each source’s **own grid with its own weights**; regrid to the WOA 1° grid only for Figure 1 and the cell-by-cell comparison metrics, and state which numbers come from own grids versus the common grid.",
        "For horizontal regridding of `tos` to the 1° grid, `regrid_horizontal` method `'conservative'` is the right choice before area-weighted comparison; state the regridding method because regridded RMSE/correlation depend on it."
      ]
    },
