      "reason": "The models are said to be on their own native grids, and this fragment matters because GFDL-ESM4 is locally on `gr` while CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are on `gn`, which affects masks and interpretation of “native-grid” results.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 `tos` is already `grid_label = gr` on a 1×1 degree archive grid, so its “own-grid” global mean is on that regridded archive grid rather than the model’s native tripolar grid; state this caveat in the answer."
      ]
    },
